#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:185
msgid "NClay vs CClay"
msgstr "NClay vs CClay"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:185
msgid ""
"Diagram of number of clay particles per liter as a function of the clay "
"concentration. Note that even 1 NTU water has millions of primary particles "
"per liter."
msgstr ""
"Diagrama del número de partículas de arcilla por litro en función de la "
"concentración de arcilla. Ten en cuenta que incluso 1 NTU de agua tiene "
"millones de partículas primarias por litro."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:187
msgid ""
"The next step is to calculate the separation distance between the clay "
"particles over this range of clay concentrations using Equation "
":eq:`eq_spacing_of_diameter`."
msgstr ""
"El siguiente paso es calcular la distancia de separación entre las "
"partículas de arcilla en este rango de concentraciones de arcilla usando la "
"ecuación :eq:`eq_spacing_of_diameter`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:189
msgid ""
"`Colab worksheet plot the separation distances "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1HhsaTHEzVKtkoiCQF-"
"XnD0ssGJ93DsXn#scrollTo=53IFiKIAsZdK&line=9&uniqifier=1>`_"
msgstr ""
"`hoja de trabajo de Colab traza las distancias de separación "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1HhsaTHEzVKtkoiCQF-"
"XnD0ssGJ93DsXn#scrollTo=53IFiKIAsZdK&line=9&uniqifier=1>`_"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:199
msgid "LambdaClay vs CClay"
msgstr "LambdaClay vs CClay"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:199
msgid ""
"The clay separation distance varies with the cube root of the concentration "
"and thus varies over a relatively narrow range (0.07 mm to 0.7 mm) while the"
" turbidity varies from 1 to 1000 NTU."
msgstr ""
"La distancia de separación de la arcilla varía con la raíz cúbica de la "
"concentración y, por tanto, varía en un rango relativamente estrecho (0,07 "
"mm a 0,7 mm), mientras que la turbidez varía de 1 a 1000 NTU."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:201
msgid ""
"Given this range of particle separation distances the next question is "
"whether transport of these particles relative to each other is driven by "
"inertial or viscous dominated processes. Turbulent eddies devolve into "
"smaller and smaller eddies until viscosity finally kills them. Viscosity "
"damps out the effects of inertia at the inner viscous length scale.  Higher "
"intensity turbulence can generate more energetic small eddies and can resist"
" the effects of viscosity longer. Thus the inner viscous length scale "
"decreases as the turbulent energy dissipation rate increases."
msgstr ""
"Dado este rango de distancias de separación de partículas, la siguiente "
"cuestión es si el transporte de estas partículas entre sí está impulsado por"
" procesos inerciales o dominados por viscosidad. Los remolinos turbulentos "
"se reducen a remolinos cada vez más pequeños hasta que la viscosidad "
"finalmente los mata. La viscosidad amortigua los efectos de la inercia en la"
" escala interior de longitud viscosa. Turbulencias de mayor intensidad "
"pueden generar pequeños remolinos más energéticos y resistir los efectos de "
"la viscosidad durante más tiempo. Así, la escala de longitud viscosa interna"
" disminuye a medida que aumenta la tasa de disipación de energía turbulenta."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:203
msgid ""
"The Camp-Stein velocity gradient  (see Equation :eq:`G_Camp_Stein`) used for"
" flocculators varies from about 20 to 300 Hz. We will use the inner viscous "
"length scale, Equation :eq:`eq_inner_viscous_length` to determine whether "
"viscous or inertial transport dominates particle collisions in surface water"
" treatment given the range of particle separation distances (see "
":numref:`figure_LambdaClay_vs_CClay`)."
msgstr ""
"El gradiente de velocidad de Camp-Stein (véase la Ecuación "
":eq:`G_Camp_Stein`) usado para floculadores varía entre aproximadamente 20 y"
" 300 Hz. Utilizaremos la escala interior de longitud viscosa, Ecuación "
":eq:`eq_inner_viscous_length` para determinar si el transporte viscoso o "
"inercial domina las colisiones de partículas en la superficie tratamiento de"
" agua dado el rango de distancias de separación de partículas (véase "
":numref:`figure_LambdaClay_vs_CClay`)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:205
msgid ""
"`Colab worksheet to plot the inner viscous length scale "
"<https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1HhsaTHEzVKtkoiCQF-"
"XnD0ssGJ93DsXn#scrollTo=naHLmCCWsIRt&line=8&uniqifier=1>`_"
msgstr ""
"`hoja de trabajo de Colab para graficar la escala interior de longitud "
"viscosa <https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1HhsaTHEzVKtkoiCQF-"
"XnD0ssGJ93DsXn#scrollTo=naHLmCCWsIRt&line=8&uniqifier=1>`_"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:215
msgid "inner viscous vs G"
msgstr "viscoso interior vs G"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:215
msgid ""
"The inner viscous length scale is approximately 3 to 10 mm for velocity "
"gradients that are typically used in flocculators. Clay separation distances"
" are smaller than the inner viscous length scale and thus viscous shear "
"dominates particle collisions in flocculation."
msgstr ""
"La escala de longitud viscosa interna es aproximadamente de 3 a 10 mm para "
"gradientes de velocidad que se utilizan típicamente en floculadores. Las "
"distancias de separación de arcilla son menores que la escala de longitud "
"viscosa interior y, por tanto, el cizallamiento viscoso domina las "
"colisiones de partículas en floculación."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:217
msgid ""
"By comparing :numref:`figure_LambdaClay_vs_CClay` and "
":numref:`figure_innerviscous_vs_G` it is apparent that the particle "
"separation distances commonly found in surface water treatment plants are "
"much smaller than the inner viscous length scale for all practical "
"flocculation velocity gradients. Thus viscosity will dominate the "
"flocculation process. This key insight reveals why turbulent flow "
"flocculators have been designed using the dimensionless grouping :math:`G "
"\\theta` which is fundamentally :math:`\\sqrt\\frac{\\epsilon}{\\nu} "
"\\theta`. Given that flocculation is viscous dominated implies that the "
"flocculation process will slow down as the temperature increases and the "
"viscosity increases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:219
msgid ""
"The flocculation model (see Equation :eq:`CPlamint`) reveals that the "
"velocity gradient multiplied by the residence time in the flocculator will "
"determine the final spacing between the primary particles. Our goal is to "
"maximize the spacing between particles and thus to minimize the number of "
"particles and potential pathogens in our drinking water."
msgstr ""
"El modelo de floculación (véase la Ecuación :eq:`CPlamint`) revela que el "
"gradiente de velocidad multiplicado por el tiempo de residencia en el "
"floculador determinará el espaciamiento final entre las partículas "
"primarias. Nuestro objetivo es maximizar el espaciamiento entre partículas y"
" así minimizar el número de partículas y posibles patógenos en nuestra agua "
"potable."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:221
msgid ""
"There are diminishing returns on investment in larger flocculators to "
"produce cleaner water because the time between collisions increases as the "
"primary particles are spaced further apart. Eventually other processes  "
"including fluidized floc filters (floc filters), plate settlers, and sand-"
"floc filter (stacked rapid sand filter) are able to reduce the primary "
"particle concentration at a lower cost."
msgstr ""
"Hay rendimientos decrecientes de la inversión en floculadores grandes para "
"producir agua más limpia porque el tiempo entre colisiones aumenta a medida "
"que las partículas primarias se separan más. Finalmente, otros procesos, "
"incluidos filtros flócs fluidizados (filtros floc), sedimentadores de placas"
" y filtro de flóculos de arena ( filtro de arena rápidas apiladas), logran "
"reducir la concentración de partículas primarias a un coste menor."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:224
msgid ""
"Collision Potential, :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`, and Energy Dissipation "
"Rate, :math:`\\varepsilon`"
msgstr ""
"Potencial de colisión, :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`y tasa de disipación de "
"energía, :math:`\\varepsilon`"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:226
msgid ""
"Collision potential :math:`(\\tilde{G} \\theta)` represents the number of "
"potential particle collisions in a volume of fluid. It is a *dimensionless* "
"parameter which is a logical design parameter for flocculators; large "
":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta` values indicate lots of collisions (good) while "
"small values indicate fewer collisions (not so good). AguaClara flocculators"
" usually aim for a collision potential of :math:`(\\tilde{G} \\theta) = "
"37,000`, which has worked well in AguaClara plants historically. However, "
"this value may change as research continues. The value for collision "
"potential is obtained by multiplying :math:`\\tilde{G}`, a parameter for "
"average fluid shear with units of :math:`\\frac{1}{[T]}`, and "
":math:`\\theta` , the residence time of water in the flocculator, with units"
" of ::math:`[T]` . :math:`\\theta` is intuitive to measure, calculate, and "
"understand. :math:`\\tilde{G}` is a bit more difficult."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:230
msgid ""
"In any control volume or reactor, the total energy dissipated is equal to "
"the mechanical energy that is converted to heat, :math:`g h_L`. The amount "
"of time required to dissipate that energy is the residence time of the water"
" in the reactor, :math:`\\theta`."
msgstr ""
"En cualquier volumen de control o reactor, la energía total disipada es "
"igual a la energía mecánica que se convierte en calor, :math:`g h_L`. El "
"tiempo necesario para disipar esa energía es el tiempo de residencia del "
"agua en el reactor, :math:`\\theta`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:232
msgid "\\bar \\varepsilon = \\frac{g h_L}{\\theta}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:237
msgid ""
"Note that the equation above is for :math:`\\bar \\varepsilon`, not "
":math:`\\varepsilon`. Since the head loss term we are using, :math:`h_L`, "
"occurs over the entire reactor, it can only be used to find an average "
"energy dissipation rate for the entire reactor. Combining the equations "
"above, :math:`G = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\varepsilon}{\\nu}}` and :math:`\\bar "
"\\varepsilon = \\frac{g h_L}{\\theta}`, we can get an equation for "
":math:`\\tilde{G}` in terms of easily measurable parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:239
msgid "\\tilde{G} = \\sqrt{\\frac{g h_L}{\\nu \\theta}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:243
msgid ""
"We can use this to obtain a final equation for collision potential of a "
"reactor:"
msgstr ""
"Podemos usar esto para obtener una ecuación final para el potencial de "
"colisión de un reactor:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:245
msgid "\\tilde{G} \\theta = \\sqrt{\\frac{g h_L \\theta}{\\nu}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:250
msgid ""
"**Note:** When we say :math:`G \\theta` we are almost always referring to "
":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`."
msgstr ""
"**Nota:** Cuando decimos :math:`G \\theta` casi siempre nos referimos a "
":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:252
msgid ""
"The head loss for a flocculator can be estimated quickly based on the basis "
"of design values of :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta` and :math:`\\tilde{G}`. "
"Rearrange Equation :eq:`Gtheta_of_hL` to obtain"
msgstr ""
"La pérdida de carga de un floculador puede estimarse rápidamente basándose "
"en los valores de diseño de :math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta` y :math:`\\tilde{G}`."
" Reorganizar la ecuación :eq:`Gtheta_of_hL` para obtener"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:254
msgid "h_L = \\frac{\\tilde{G} \\theta \\nu \\tilde{G}}{g}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:260
msgid ""
"The head loss increases with the required collision potential "
":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta` and it also increases with the velocity gradient."
" Cold water also requires more head loss due to the increased viscosity and "
"hence more energy is required to deform the fluid and achieve the target "
"collision potential."
msgstr ""
"El pérdida de carga aumenta con el potencial de colisión requerido "
":math:`\\tilde{G} \\theta` y también aumenta con el gradiente de velocidad. "
"El agua fría también requiere más pérdida de carga debido al aumento de la "
"viscosidad y, por tanto, se requiere más energía para deformar el fluido y "
"alcanzar el potencial de colisión objetivo."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:263
msgid "Generating Head Loss with Baffles"
msgstr "Generación de pérdida de carga con deflectores"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:266
msgid "**What are Baffles?**"
msgstr "**¿Qué son los deflectores?**"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:268
msgid ""
"Now that we know how to measure collision potential with head loss, we need "
"a way to actually generate head loss. While both major or minor losses can "
"be the design basis, it generally makes more sense to use major losses only "
"for very low-flow flocculation (lab-scale) and minor losses for higher "
"flows, as flocculation with minor losses tends to be more space-efficient. "
"Since this book focuses on town and village-scale water treatment (5 L/S to "
"120 L/S), we will use minor losses as our design basis."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que sabemos cómo medir el potencial de colisión con pérdida de carga, "
"necesitamos una forma de generar realmente pérdida de carga. Aunque tanto "
"pérdidas mayores como menores pueden ser la base de diseño, generalmente "
"tiene más sentido usar pérdidas mayores solo para floculaciones de muy bajo "
"flujo (a escala de laboratorio) y pérdidas menores para caudales mayores, ya"
" que la floculación con pérdidas menores tiende a ser más eficiente en "
"espacio. Dado que este libro se centra en tratamiento de agua a escala de "
"ciudad y pueblo (5 L/S a 120 L/S), utilizaremos pérdidas menores como base "
"de diseño."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:270
msgid ""
"To generate minor losses, we need to create flow expansions. AguaClara does "
"this with **baffles**, which are obstructions in the channel of a "
"flocculator to force the flow to switch directions by 180°. Baffles in "
"AguaClara plants are plastic sheets, and all of the baffles in one "
"flocculator channel are connected to form a **baffle module.** "
":numref:`figure_AC_flocculator` shows an AguaClara flocculator and "
":numref:`figure_baffle_module` shows the assembly of a baffle module."
msgstr ""
"Para generar pérdidas menores, necesitamos crear expansiones de flujo. "
"AguaClara hace esto con **deflectores**, que son obstrucciones en el canal "
"de un floculador para forzar el flujo a cambiar de dirección en 180°. Los "
"deflectores en las plantas de AguaClara son láminas de plástico, y todos los"
" deflectores en un canal de floculador están conectados para formar un "
"**módulo de floculador.** :numref:`figure_AC_flocculator` muestra un "
"floculador AguaClara y :numref:`figure_baffle_module` muestra el ensamblaje "
"de un módulo de deflector."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:279
msgid "AC Flocculator"
msgstr "Floculador de CA"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:279
msgid ""
"Clockwise from the top left the images show: the outline of the entire "
"flocculator, some top and bottom baffles in the channels, the 4 flocculator "
"channels in this flocculator, and the flow path of water through the "
"flocculator"
msgstr ""
"En sentido horario desde la esquina superior izquierda las imágenes "
"muestran: el contorno de todo el floculador, algunos deflectores superior e "
"inferior en los canales, los 4 canales del floculador en este floculador y "
"el camino del flujo del agua a través del floculador"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:288
msgid "this image shows the floc baffle module out of the water within a plant."
msgstr ""
"Esta imagen muestra el módulo deflector FLOC fuera del agua dentro de una "
"planta."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:288
msgid ""
"Before being inserted into the flocculator channel, the baffle module is "
"constructed as a unit as shown above."
msgstr ""
"Antes de insertarse en el canal floculador, el módulo de deflector se "
"construye como una unidad como se muestra arriba."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:290
msgid ""
"AguaClara flocculators, like the one pictured above, are called **horizontal"
" vertical flow flocculators** (see :numref:`figure_HVflocculator`)."
msgstr ""
"Los floculadores AguaClara, como el que se muestra en la imagen anterior, se"
" llaman **floculadores de flujo vertical horizontal** (véase "
":numref:`figure_HVflocculator`)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:293
msgid "**Finding the Minor Loss of a Baffle**"
msgstr "**Encontrando la pérdida menor de un deflector**"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:295
msgid ""
"Before beginning this section, it is important to understand how water flows"
" through a baffled flocculator. This flow path is shown in "
":numref:`figure_flocculator_flow`. Take note of the thin red arrows; they "
"indicate the compression of the flow around a baffle."
msgstr ""
"Antes de comenzar esta sección, es importante entender cómo fluye el agua a "
"través de un floculador con deflector. Este camino de flujo se muestra en "
":numref:`figure_flocculator_flow`. Fíjate en las finas flechas rojas; "
"indican la compresión del flujo alrededor de un deflector."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:304
msgid "flocculator flow image"
msgstr "Imagen del flujo del floculador"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:304
msgid "Flow path through a vertical flow hydraulic flocculator"
msgstr "Trayectoria de flujo a través de un floculador hidráulico de flujo vertical"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:306
msgid ""
"Since baffles are the source of head loss via minor losses, we need to find "
"the minor loss coefficient of one baffle if we want to be able to quantify "
"its head loss. To do this, we apply fluid mechanics intuition and check it "
"against a computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulation. Flow around a 90° "
"bend has a *vena contracta* value of :math:`\\Pi_{vc} = 0.611` as given by "
"Equation :eq:`theta_slot_vena_contracta_analytical`. Flow around a 180° bend"
" therefore has a value of :math:`\\color{red}{\\Pi_{vc}^{baffle} = "
"\\Pi_{vc}^2 = 0.373}`. This number is roughly confirmed with CFD, as shown "
"in the image below."
msgstr ""
"Dado que los deflectores son la fuente de pérdida de carga a través de "
"pérdidas menores, necesitamos encontrar el coeficiente de pérdida menor de "
"uno de los deflectores si queremos poder cuantificar su pérdida de carga. "
"Para ello, aplicamos la intuición de mecánica de fluidos y la comparamos con"
" una simulación de dinámica de fluidos computacional (CFD). El flujo "
"alrededor de una curva de 90° tiene un valor de *vena contracta* de "
":math:`\\Pi_{vc} = 0.611` dado por la ecuación "
":eq:`theta_slot_vena_contracta_analytical`. Por tanto, el flujo alrededor de"
" una curva de 180° tiene un valor de :math:`\\color{red}{\\Pi_{vc}^{baffle} "
"= \\Pi_{vc}^2 = 0.373}`. Este número se confirma aproximadamente con CFD, "
"como se muestra en la imagen de abajo."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:315
msgid "CFD vc baffle"
msgstr "Deflector de VC CFD"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:315
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The 180° bend at the end of a baffle results in a dramatic flow contraction "
"with all of the flow passing through less than 40% of the space between the "
"baffles."
msgstr ""
"La curva de 180° al final de un deflector provoca una contracción dramática "
"del flujo, con todo el flujo pasando por menos del 40% del espacio entre los"
" deflectores."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:319
#, python-format
msgid ""
"We can therefore state with reasonable accuracy that, when most contracted, "
"the flow around a baffle goes through 37.3% of the area it does when "
"expanded, or :math:`A_{contracted} = \\Pi_{vc}^{baffle} A_{expanded}`. "
"Through the `:ref:`third form of the minor loss equation "
"<heading_minor_losses>`, :math:`h_e = K \\frac{\\bar v_{out}^2}{2g}` and its"
" definition of the minor loss coefficient, :math:`K = \\left( "
"\\frac{A_{out}}{A_{in}} -1 \\right)^2`, we can determine the minimum minor "
"loss coefficient for flow around a single baffle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:321
msgid ""
"K_{baffle_{min}} = \\left( \\frac{A_{expanded}}{A_{contracted}} -1 "
"\\right)^2\n"
"\n"
"= \\left( \\frac{1}{\\Pi_{vc}^{baffle}} -1 \\right)^2\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"= \\left( \\frac{1}{0.373} -1 \\right)^2\n"
"\n"
"\\color{red} {= 2.82}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:333
msgid ""
"This :math:`K_{baffle_{min}}` has been used to design flocculators in "
"AguaClara plants until 2021. The plant at Gracias revealed that the observed"
" head loss was greater than predicted.  `This paper by Haarhoff in 1998 "
"<https://iwaponline.com/aqua/article/47/3/142/31711/Design-of-around-the-"
"end-hydraulic-flocculators>`_  (DOI: 10.2166/aqua.1998.20), the "
":math:`K_{baffle}` values found are context dependent and empirically based."
" Further analysis of how :math:`K_{baffle}` varies with the geometry of the "
"flocculator is given in the section on "
":ref:`heading_Baffle_Loss_Coefficient`."
msgstr ""
"Este :math:`K_{baffle_{min}}` se ha utilizado para diseñar floculadores en "
"plantas de AguaClara hasta 2021. La planta de Gracias reveló que el pérdida "
"de carga observado era mayor de lo previsto. `Este artículo de Haarhoff en "
"1998 <https://iwaponline.com/aqua/article/47/3/142/31711/Design-of-around-"
"the-end-hydraulic-flocculators>`_ (DOI: 10.2166/aqua.1998.20), los valores "
"de :math:`K_{baffle}` encontrados dependen del contexto y se basan "
"empíricamente. Un análisis adicional de cómo varía :math:`K_{baffle}` con la"
" geometría del floculador se ofrece en la sección sobre "
":ref:`heading_Baffle_Loss_Coefficient`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:335
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`K_baffle_min` doesn't account for the fact that for a series "
"of baffles (or flow contractions) the flow might not be able to fully expand"
" before entering the next baffle (or contraction). The distance required for"
" the contracted flow to expand can be estimated from jet equations (see "
"section on :ref:`Baffle Minor Loss "
"Coefficient<heading_Baffle_Loss_Coefficient>` for an estimate of how the "
"minor loss coefficient increases when the flow doesn't fully expand)."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`K_baffle_min` no tiene en cuenta el hecho de que, para una "
"serie de deflectores (o contracciones de flujo), el flujo puede no ser capaz"
" de expandirse completamente antes de entrar en el siguiente deflector (o "
"contracción). La distancia necesaria para que el flujo contraído se expanda "
"puede estimarse a partir de ecuaciones de chorro (véase la sección sobre "
":ref:`Baffle Minor Loss Coefficient<heading_Baffle_Loss_Coefficient>` para "
"una estimación de cómo aumenta el coeficiente de pérdida menor cuando el "
"flujo no se expande completamente)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:338
msgid "Flocculator Efficiency"
msgstr "Eficiencia de floculadores"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:340
msgid ""
"When designing an effective and efficient flocculator, there are two main "
"problems that we seek to avoid:"
msgstr ""
"Al diseñar un floculador eficaz y eficiente, hay dos problemas principales "
"que intentamos evitar:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:342
msgid ""
"Having certain sections in the flocculator with such high local "
":math:`\\tilde{G}` values that our big, fluffy flocs are sheared apart into "
"smaller flocs."
msgstr ""
"Tener ciertas secciones en el floculador con valores de :math:`\\tilde{G}` "
"locales tan altos que nuestros flóclos grandes y esponjosos se deshacen en "
"flóclos más pequeños."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:343
msgid ""
"Having dead space. Dead space means volume within the flocculator that is "
"not being used to facilitate collisions. Dead space occurs after the flow "
"has fully expanded from flowing around a baffle and before it reaches the "
"next baffle."
msgstr ""
"Tener espacio muerto. Espacio muerto significa volumen dentro del floculador"
" que no se está utilizando para facilitar colisiones. El espacio muerto "
"ocurre después de que el flujo se ha expandido completamente al fluir "
"alrededor de un deflector y antes de llegar al siguiente deflector."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:345
msgid "Fortunately for us, both problems can be quantified with a single ratio:"
msgstr ""
"Afortunadamente para nosotros, ambos problemas pueden cuantificarse con una "
"única razón:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:347
msgid "\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}} = \\frac{G_{max}}{\\tilde{G}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:352
msgid ""
"High values of :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}` occur when one or both of"
" the previous problems is present. If certain sections in the flocculator "
"have very high local :math:`G` values, then :math:`G_{max}` becomes large. "
"If the flocculator has a lot of dead space, then :math:`\\tilde{G}` becomes "
"small. Either way, :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}` becomes larger."
msgstr ""
"Valores altos de :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}` se producen cuando uno "
"o ambos problemas anteriores están presentes. Si ciertas secciones del "
"floculador tienen valores de :math:`G` local muy altos, entonces "
":math:`G_{max}` se vuelve grande. Si el floculador tiene mucho espacio "
"muerto, entonces :math:`\\tilde{G}` se vuelve pequeño. En cualquier caso, "
":math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}` se hace más grande."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:354
msgid ""
"**Note:** Recall the relationship between :math:`G` and :math:`\\varepsilon`"
" : :math:`G = \\sqrt{ \\frac{\\varepsilon}{\\nu} }`. From this relationship,"
" we can see that :math:`G \\propto \\sqrt{\\varepsilon}`. Thus, by defining"
"  :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}`, we can also define a ratio for max to"
" average energy dissipation rate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:356
msgid ""
"\\Pi_{\\bar \\varepsilon}^{\\varepsilon_{max}} = \\left( "
"\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}} \\right)^2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:360
msgid ""
"Therefore, by making our :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}` as small as "
"possible, we can be sure that our flocculator is efficient, and we no longer"
" have to account for the previously mentioned problems. `A paper by Haarhoff"
" and van der Walt in 2001 "
"<https://iwaponline.com/aqua/article/50/3/149/30498/Towards-optimal-design-"
"parameters-for-around-the>`_ (DOI: 10.2166/aqua.2001.0014) uses CFD to show "
"that the minimum :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}}` attainable in a "
"hydraulic flocculator is :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}} = \\sqrt{2} "
"\\approx 1.4`, which means that :math:`\\Pi_{\\bar "
"\\varepsilon}^{\\varepsilon_{max}} = \\left( \\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}} "
"\\right)^2 \\approx 2`. So how do we optimize an AguaClara flocculator to "
"make sure :math:`\\Pi_{\\tilde{G}}^{G_{max}} = \\sqrt{2}`?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:362
msgid "We define and optimize a performance metric:"
msgstr "Definimos y optimizamos una métrica de rendimiento:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:364
msgid "\\frac{H_e}{S} = \\Pi_{H_eS}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:368
msgid ""
"Where :math:`H_e` is the distance between flow expansions in the flocculator"
" and :math:`S` is the spacing between baffles. For now, :math:`H_e` is "
"approximated as the height of water in the flocculator."
msgstr ""
"Donde :math:`H_e` es la distancia entre las expansiones del flujo en el "
"floculador y :math:`S` es el espaciado entre los deflectores. Por ahora, "
":math:`H_e` se aproxima como la altura del agua en el floculador."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:370
msgid ""
"Since :math:`G_{max}` is determined by the fluid mechanics of flow around a "
"baffle, our main concern is eliminating dead space in the flocculator. We do"
" this by placing an upper limit on :math:`\\frac{H_e}{S}`. To determine this"
" upper limit, we need to find the distance it takes for the flow to fully "
"expand after it has contracted around a baffle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:372
msgid "\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}}x = D - D_{cp}"
msgstr "\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}}x = D - D_{cp}"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:383
msgid "jet expansion in the flocculator"
msgstr "Expansión por chorro en el floculador"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:383
msgid ""
"A turbulent jet expands in width by approximately one unit for every 10 "
"units downstream (see Equation :eq:`PlaneJet_expansion`)."
msgstr ""
"Un chorro turbulento se expande en anchura aproximadamente una unidad por "
"cada 10 unidades aguas abajo (véase la ecuación :eq:`PlaneJet_expansion`)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:385
msgid ""
"Using the equation and image above, we can find the distance required for "
"the flow to fully expand around a baffle as a function of baffle spacing "
":math:`S`. We do this by substituting  :math:`D_{cp} = (0.373 S)` along with"
" :math:`D = S` to approximate how much distance, :math:`x = L_{jet}`, the "
"contracted flow has to cover."
msgstr ""
"Usando la ecuación y la imagen anteriores, podemos encontrar la distancia "
"necesaria para que el flujo se expanda completamente alrededor de un "
"deflector en función del espaciado del deflector :math:`S`. Lo hacemos "
"sustituyendo  :math:`D_{cp} = (0.373 S)` junto con :math:`D = S` para "
"aproximar cuánta distancia, :math:`x = L_{jet}`, debe cubrir el flujo "
"contraído."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:387
msgid "\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}} L_{jet} = S - (0.373 S)"
msgstr "\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}} L_{jet} = S - (0,373 S)"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:391
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}}` is the dimensionless rate of expansion "
"for the jet that has a baffle on one side."
msgstr ""
"donde :math:`\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}}` es la tasa adimensional de expansión "
"del chorro que tiene un deflector en un lado."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:393
msgid "L_{jet_{max}} = \\frac{0.627 S}{\\Pi_{BaffleJet_{exp}}} = 10.8S"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:397
msgid ""
"This gives a rough estimate of the maximum distance between flow expansions "
"while ensuring that there are no zones of low turbulence in the flocculator."
" The relationship between :math:`L_{jet_{max}}` and the flocculator geometry"
" is given in Equation :eq:`L_jet`."
msgstr ""
"Esto proporciona una estimación aproximada de la distancia máxima entre "
"expansiones de flujo, asegurando que no haya zonas de baja turbulencia en el"
" floculador. La relación entre :math:`L_{jet_{max}}` y la geometría del "
"floculador se da en la Ecuación :eq:`L_jet`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:406
msgid "CFD baffle image"
msgstr "Imagen del deflector CFD"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:406
msgid ""
"High :math:`\\frac{H_e}{S}` ratios result in flocculator zones with low "
"velocity gradients that don't contribute effectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:415
msgid "CFD full channel"
msgstr "Canal completo CFD"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:415
msgid ""
"Each bend creates a flow contraction and when the flow expands it converts "
"kinetic energy into turbulent eddies and fluid deformation. The fluid "
"deformation is what ultimately creates collisions between particles."
msgstr ""
"Cada curvatura crea una contracción del flujo y, cuando el flujo se expande,"
" convierte la energía cinética en remolinos turbulentos y deformación del "
"fluido. La deformación del fluido es lo que, en última instancia, genera "
"colisiones entre partículas."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:417
msgid ""
"The lowest functional :math:`\\frac{H_e}{S}` ratio, "
":math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}` is an important constraint for the design of "
"flocculators that have vertical flow between baffles because it sets the "
"minimum water depth in the flocculator channel. The absolute minimum value "
"of :math:`\\frac{H_e}{S}` is set by the flow geometry to ensure that water "
"can't flow straight through the flocculator without going back and forth or "
"up and down around the baffles. This short circuiting would depend on the "
"slot width, defined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:419
msgid ""
"Slot width is the distance between the water level and the top of an upper "
"baffle (which is the same distance between the flocculator floor and the "
"bottom of an upper baffle). This distance is referred to as the slot width "
"(`Haarhoff 1998 <http://aqua.iwaponline.com/content/47/3/142>`_)  DOI: "
"10.2166/aqua.1998.20\") and is defined by the slot width ratio, which "
"describes the slot width as a function of baffle spacing :math:`S`. Slot "
"width is shown in the following image:"
msgstr ""
"El ancho de ranura es la distancia entre el nivel del agua y la parte "
"superior de un deflector superior (que es la misma distancia entre el suelo "
"del floculador y la parte inferior de un deflector superior). Esta distancia"
" se denomina ancho de ranura (`Haarhoff 1998 "
"<http://aqua.iwaponline.com/content/47/3/142>`_) DOI: "
"10.2166/aqua.1998.20\") y se define por la relación de ancho de ranura, que "
"describe el ancho de ranura en función del espaciado del deflector "
":math:`S`. El ancho de ranura se muestra en la siguiente imagen:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:428
msgid "image showing the dimensiond of spacing within the flocculator"
msgstr "imagen que muestra la dimensión del espaciamiento dentro del floculador"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:428
msgid ""
"The space between the bottom of the upper baffle and the floor of the "
"flocculator is defined as the slot width."
msgstr ""
"El espacio entre la parte inferior del deflector superior y el suelo del "
"floculador se define como el ancho de ranura."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:430
msgid ""
"AguaClara uses a slot width ratio of 1 for its flocculators. This number has"
" been the topic of much hydraulic flocculation research, and values between "
"1 and 1.5 are generally accepted for hydraulic flocculators. See the "
"following paper and book respectively for more data on slot width ratios and"
" other hydraulic flocculator parameters: :cite:`floc-haarhoff_design_1998`, "
":cite:`floc-schulz_surface_1984`. We base our slot width ratio of 1 on "
"research done by :cite:`floc-haarhoff_towards_2001` on optimizing hydraulic "
"flocculator parameters to maximize flocculator efficiency."
msgstr ""
"AguaClara utiliza una relación de ancho de ranura de 1 para sus "
"floculadores. Este número ha sido objeto de mucha investigación sobre "
"floculaciones hidráulicas, y valores entre 1 y 1,5 son generalmente "
"aceptados para floculadores hidráulicos. Consulte el siguiente artículo y "
"libro respectivamente para más datos sobre las relaciones de ancho de ranura"
" y otros parámetros de floculadores hidráulicos: :cite:`floc-"
"haarhoff_design_1998`, :cite:`floc-schulz_surface_1984`. Basamos nuestra "
"relación de ancho de ranura de 1 en investigaciones realizadas por :cite"
":`floc-haarhoff_towards_2001` sobre la optimización de parámetros de "
"floculadores hidráulicos para maximizar la eficiencia de los floculadores."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:432
msgid ""
"The minimum :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` allowable depends on the slot with ratio. If"
" :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` is less than twice the slot width ratio, the water "
"would flow straight through the flocculator without having to bend around "
"the baffles. This means that the flocculator would not be generating almost "
"any head loss, and the top and bottom of the flocculator will largely be "
"dead space. See the following image for an example:"
msgstr ""
"El :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` mínimo permitido depende de la ranura con la "
"relación. Si :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` es menor del doble de la relación de ancho "
"de ranura, el agua fluiría directamente a través del floculador sin tener "
"que doblarse alrededor de los deflectores. Esto significa que el floculador "
"no generaría casi ningún pérdida de carga, y la parte superior e inferior "
"del floculador serán en gran parte espacios muertos. Véase la siguiente "
"imagen como ejemplo:"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:441
msgid "minimum H S ratio"
msgstr "Ratio mínima H S"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:441
msgid ""
"The minimum :math:`\\frac{H_e}{S}` ratio is set by the need to prevent short"
" circuiting through the flocculator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:443
msgid ""
"Thus, :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}` should be at least twice the slot width "
"ratio, :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}} = 2`. Historically, AguaClara plants have "
"been designed using :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}} = 3`. This adds a safety factor"
" of sorts, ensuring that the flow does not short-circuit through the "
"flocculator and also allowing more space for the flow to expand after each "
"contraction."
msgstr ""
"Por tanto, :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}}` deberían tener al menos el doble de la "
"relación de ancho de ranura, :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}} = 2`. Históricamente, "
"las plantas AguaClara se han diseñado usando :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}} = 3`. "
"Esto añade un factor de seguridad, asegurando que el flujo no se provoque un"
" cortocircuito a través del floculador y también permitiendo más espacio "
"para que el flujo se expanda tras cada contracción."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:445
msgid "\\Pi_{H_eS_{min}} = \\frac{H_e}{S} = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:449
msgid ""
"Although this value of :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` meets the geometric constraints "
"it is not necessarily the best design since the flow doesn't come close to "
"fully expanding between contractions. This results in a much higher baffle "
"loss coefficient and a higher level of uncertainty of the exact value of "
"that loss coefficient. Thus we recommend using higher values of "
":math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` when possible."
msgstr ""
"Aunque este valor de :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` cumple con las restricciones "
"geométricas, no es necesariamente el mejor diseño, ya que el flujo no se "
"acerca a expandirse completamente entre contracciones. Esto resulta en un "
"coeficiente de pérdida de baffle mucho más alto y un mayor nivel de "
"incertidumbre sobre el valor exacto de ese coeficiente de pérdida. Por ello,"
" recomendamos usar valores más altos de :math:`\\Pi_{H_eS}` cuando sea "
"posible."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:452
msgid "Flocculator Geometry"
msgstr "Geometría de floculadores"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:454
msgid ""
"The geometry of hydraulic flocculators changes rather dramatically as the "
"flow rate increases from a fraction of a L/s up to thousands of L/s. The "
"transition from one geometry to another is dependent on economic factors, "
"fabrication constraints, and integration with the rest of the plant design. "
"Thus the flow transition between each of the distinct geometries will evolve"
" as design optimization progresses. Flows between 0.5 L/s and 20 L/s are "
"efficiently handled by a Vertical-Horizontal flow flocculator as shown in "
":numref:`figure_VHflocculator`."
msgstr ""
"La geometría de los floculadores hidráulicos cambia bastante drásticamente a"
" medida que la caudal aumenta de una fracción de L/s a miles de L/s. La "
"transición de una geometría a otra depende de factores económicos, "
"restricciones de fabricación y de la integración con el resto del diseño de "
"la planta. Así, la transición de flujo entre cada una de las geometrías "
"distintas evolucionará a medida que avanza la optimización del diseño. Los "
"flujos entre 0,5 L/s y 20 L/s son gestionados eficientemente por un "
"floculador de flujo vertical-horizontal, como se muestra en "
":numref:`figure_VHflocculator`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:463
msgid "vertical - horizontal flocculator"
msgstr "Floculador vertical - horizontal"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:463
msgid ""
"The vertical-horizontal flocculator has vertical flow in the channels and "
"horizontal flow between baffles. This design is for 6 L/s with 23.5 cm of "
"head loss."
msgstr ""
"El floculador vertical-horizontal tiene flujo vertical en los canales y "
"flujo horizontal entre deflectores. Este diseño es para 6 L/s con 23,5 cm de"
" pérdida de carga."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:465
msgid ""
"As the flows increase the spacing between baffles grows larger and a "
"vertical-horizontal flocculator would need to be very deep in order to "
"accommodate a reasonable number of baffle spaces per channel. The geometry "
"switches to horizontal-vertical for flows between about 20 and 200 L/s as "
"shown in :numref:`figure_HVflocculator`."
msgstr ""
"A medida que aumentan los flujos, el espaciado entre los defletores se hace "
"más grande y un floculador vertical-horizontal tendría que ser muy profundo "
"para acomodar un número razonable de espacios de deflectores por canal. La "
"geometría cambia a horizontal-vertical para flujos entre unos 20 y 200 L/s, "
"como se muestra en :numref:`figure_HVflocculator`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:474 ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:486
msgid "horizontal-vertical flocculator"
msgstr "Floculador horizontal-vertical"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:474
msgid ""
"The horizontal-vertical flocculator has horizontal flow in the channels and "
"vertical flow between baffles.This design is for 60 L/s with 1 m wide "
"channels and 25 cm of head loss."
msgstr ""
"El floculador horizontal-vertical tiene flujo horizontal en los canales y "
"flujo vertical entre deflectores. Este diseño es para 60 L/s con canales de "
"1 m de ancho y 25 cm de pérdida de carga."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:477
msgid ""
"As the flow increases above 200 L/s the required depth to accommodate a "
"reasonable H/S ratio will exceed the desired depth (from a construction and "
"maintenance perspective) and the optimal design will switch to a horizontal-"
"horizontal flocculator as shown in :numref:`figure_HHflocculator`."
msgstr ""
"A medida que el caudal supera los 200 L/s, la profundidad requerida para "
"acomodar una relación H/S razonable superará la profundidad deseada (desde "
"la perspectiva de construcción y mantenimiento) y el diseño óptimo cambiará "
"a un floculador horizontal-horizontal como se muestra en "
":numref:`figure_HHflocculator`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Intro.rst:486
msgid ""
"The horizontal-vertical flocculator has horizontal flow in the channels and "
"vertical flow between baffles. This design is for a 500 L/s flow with 29 cm "
"of head loss. The channels are 2.6 m deep."
msgstr ""
"El floculador horizontal-vertical tiene flujo horizontal en los canales y "
"flujo vertical entre deflectores. Este diseño es para un flujo de 500 L/s "
"con 29 cm de pérdida de carga. Los canales tienen una profundidad de 2,6 m."

